[{"text":"When you square an expression with dummy indices, you must rename them first. People often do this by hand, e.g. as in","anchor":"handling-indices"},{"text":"ex1 = (FV[p, \\[Mu]] + FV[q, \\[Mu]]) FV[r, \\[Mu]] FV[r, \\[Nu]]","anchor":"cb2"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{r}^{\\mu } \\overline{r}^{\\nu } \\left(\\overline{p}^{\\mu }+\\overline{q}^{\\mu }\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb2-1"},{"text":"ex1 (ex1 /. \\[Mu] -> \\[Rho]) Contract[%]","anchor":"cb3"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{r}^{\\mu } \\left(\\overline{r}^{\\nu }\\right)^2 \\overline{r}^{\\rho } \\left(\\overline{p}^{\\mu }+\\overline{q}^{\\mu }\\right) \\left(\\overline{p}^{\\rho }+\\overline{q}^{\\rho }\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb3-2"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{r}^2 \\left(\\overline{p}\\cdot \\overline{r}+\\overline{q}\\cdot \\overline{r}\\right)^2\\]","anchor":"cb3-2"},{"text":"However, since FeynCalc 9 there is a function for that","anchor":"cb3-2"},{"text":"FCRenameDummyIndices[ex1]","anchor":"cb4"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{r}^{\\nu } \\overline{r}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$19})} \\left(\\overline{p}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$19})}+\\overline{q}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$19})}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb4-1"},{"text":"ex1 FCRenameDummyIndices[ex1] Contract[%]","anchor":"cb5"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{r}^{\\mu } \\overline{r}^{\\nu } \\overline{r}^{\\nu } \\left(\\overline{p}^{\\mu }+\\overline{q}^{\\mu }\\right) \\overline{r}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$20})} \\left(\\overline{p}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$20})}+\\overline{q}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$20})}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb5-2"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{r}^2 \\left(\\overline{p}\\cdot \\overline{r}+\\overline{q}\\cdot \\overline{r}\\right)^2\\]","anchor":"cb5-2"},{"text":"Notice that FCRenameDummyIndices does not canonicalize the indices","anchor":"cb5-2"},{"text":"FV[p, \\[Nu]] FV[q, \\[Nu]] - FV[p, \\[Mu]] FV[q, \\[Mu]] FCRenameDummyIndices[%]","anchor":"cb6"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\nu } \\overline{q}^{\\nu }-\\overline{p}^{\\mu } \\overline{q}^{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb6-2"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$22})} \\overline{q}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$22})}-\\overline{p}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$21})} \\overline{q}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$21})}\\]","anchor":"cb6-2"},{"text":"But since FeynCalc 9.1 there is a function for that too","anchor":"cb6-2"},{"text":"FV[p, \\[Nu]] FV[q, \\[Nu]] - FV[p, \\[Mu]] FV[q, \\[Mu]] FCCanonicalizeDummyIndices[%]","anchor":"cb7"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\nu } \\overline{q}^{\\nu }-\\overline{p}^{\\mu } \\overline{q}^{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb7-2"},{"text":"\\[0\\]","anchor":"cb7-2"},{"text":"Finally, often we also need to uncontract already contracted indices. This is done by Uncontract. By default, it handles only contractions with Dirac matrices and Levi-Civita tensors","anchor":"cb7-2"},{"text":"LC[][p, q, r, s] Uncontract[%, p] Uncontract[%%, p, q]","anchor":"cb8"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\overline{p}\\overline{q}\\overline{r}\\overline{s}}\\]","anchor":"cb8-3"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$31})} \\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$31})\\overline{q}\\overline{r}\\overline{s}}\\]","anchor":"cb8-3"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$33})} \\overline{q}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$32})} \\left(-\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$32})\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$33})\\overline{r}\\overline{s}}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb8-3"},{"text":"SP[p, q] Uncontract[%, p]","anchor":"cb9"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}\\cdot \\overline{q}\\]","anchor":"cb9-2"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}\\cdot \\overline{q}\\]","anchor":"cb9-2"},{"text":"To uncontract scalar products as well, use the option Pair->All","anchor":"cb9-2"},{"text":"Uncontract[%, p, Pair -> All]","anchor":"cb10"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$34})} \\overline{q}^{\\text{\\$AL}(\\text{\\$34})}\\]","anchor":"cb10-1"}]